    "bio": "A Representative from Georgia; born in Augusta, Richmond County, Ga., July 10, 1942; graduated from St. Thomas Aquinas High School, Augusta, Ga., 1960; B.S., Georgia Institute of Technology, Atlanta, Ga., 1965; M.D., Medical College of Georgia, Augusta, Ga., 1969; physician; member of the Marietta, Ga., board of education, 1993-1997; member of the Georgia state senate, 1999-2002; elected as a Republican to the One Hundred Eighth and to the five succeeding Congresses (January 3, 2003-January 3, 2015); unsuccessful candidate for nomination to the United States Senate in 2014.",
